a6=A.d8("A 58-year-old with a T6 SCI has a skin graft at the T8 dermatome bilaterally. Sensation at T8 cannot be properly tested and is marked as 0** (consider normal for classification). All other values are straightforward. No sacral sparing.",d4,A.d5(B.Y,A.bt(A.aq(b6,0,b8,d5,A.a2(["T8","0**","T9","0","T10","0"],l,l)),b7,a7,A.aq(b6,0,b8,d5,A.a2(["T8","0**","T9","0","T10","0"],l,l))),a6,B.Y),"adv-04",'Double-asterisk (**) means "consider normal" -- the value is 0 but should be treated as if it could be 2 (normal) for classification. T8 = 0** means the sensory level COULD be T8 (if T8 is considered normal) or T7 (if T8 is taken at face value). The algorithm may return variable sensory levels. This teaches how non-SCI conditions affect classification.',"Double-Asterisk Values (Consider Normal)")
