a7=A.d8("A 36-year-old sustains a T8 SCI. Sensory normal through T8 bilaterally. S4-5 light touch and pin prick are recorded as NT (patient has perianal burns preventing testing). DAP is NT. VAC is No. All LE motors 0/5.",d4,A.d5(B.eq,A.bt(A.aq(b6,0,b8,c5,A.a2(["S4_5","NT"],l,l)),b7,a8,A.aq(b6,0,b8,c5,A.a2(["S4_5","NT"],l,l))),a7,B.Y),"adv-05","When S4-5 sensation and DAP are NT, sacral sparing cannot be determined. The injury could be complete (AIS A) or incomplete (AIS B). The algorithm will return variable completeness. VAC is No, so if sacral sparing is absent this is AIS A; if present, AIS B. This teaches how untestable sacral segments create classification ambiguity.","NT at S4-5 Affecting Completeness")
